-- title:
--   Elliptic transport with coupled measures at a finite place
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ of degree $2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $v$ be a maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_K$, let $c\in (K_v)^\times$, and let $\delta\in GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, where $K_v$ denotes the $v$-adic completion. Assume the scalar matrix $c\cdot 1$ is a norm of $\delta$, i.e. $1\otimes(c\cdot 1)=y^{-1}\,N(\delta)\,y$ for some $y$, where $N(\delta)=\prod_{i<[L:K]}\sigma^i(\delta)$ is the norm string; assume further that $\delta$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate to any scalar matrix $z\cdot 1$, $z\in (L\otimes_K K_v)^\times$ (no $x$ with $z\cdot 1=x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)$). Let $\tau'$ be a Haar measure on the twisted centraliser $T'_\delta$ of $\delta$, all subgroups and groups carrying their Borel structures. Then there exist $u_0\in T'_\delta$, $\gamma_0\in GL_2(K_v)$, $y_1\in GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, a Haar measure $\tau_S$ on $S=T'_\delta\cap T'_{u_0\delta}$ and a Haar measure $\tau_T$ on the centraliser $T$ of $\gamma_0$ in $GL_2(K_v)$ such that: $\gamma_0$ is regular semisimple in the sense that $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma_0)^2-4\det(\gamma_0)$ is a unit; no conjugate $g^{-1}\gamma_0 g$ has both off-diagonal entries zero; $\gamma_0$ is a norm of $u_0\delta$, indeed $1\otimes\gamma_0=y_1^{-1}N(u_0\delta)y_1$; for every neighbourhood $W$ of $c\cdot 1$ in $GL_2(K_v)$ and every neighbourhood $V$ of $1$ in $GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ there are $u\in V\cap S$ with $N(u\delta)$ regular semisimple and a regular semisimple $\gamma\in W\cap T$ with $1\otimes\gamma=y_1^{-1}N(u\delta)y_1$, together with Haar measures $\tau_\gamma$ on the centraliser of $\gamma$ and $\tau_u$ on $T'_{u\delta}$ whose images in the ambient groups coincide with those of $\tau_T$ and $\tau_S$ respectively, which are coupled through $y_1$ (the image of $\tau_u$ under $t\mapsto y_1^{-1}ty_1$ equals the image of $\tau_\gamma$ under $m\mapsto 1\otimes m$), and such that for every locally constant compactly supported $\varphi_v:GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)\to\mathbb C$ the twisted orbital integral of $\varphi_v$ at $u\delta$ against $\tau_u$ exists; finally $S=y_1\,(1\otimes T)\,y_1^{-1}$, membership being characterised elementwise, and the image of $\tau_S$ under $s\mapsto y_1^{-1}sy_1$ equals the image of $\tau_T$ under $m\mapsto 1\otimes m$.
--
--   This is the transport half of the elliptic package at a finite place in the local analysis of base change for $GL_2$ over a quadratic extension: a $\sigma$-conjugacy class of the second kind is moved to a regular elliptic norm $\gamma_0$, the twisted centraliser is straightened to the base-change image of a torus of $GL_2(K_v)$, and Haar measures on the two sides are matched. It feeds the combined finite-place statement that adjoins the Weil-constant and volume normalisations.
